        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-16T23:07:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My goal here was to not handle the exception and let it flow.\n\n`withTimeout` creates a scope and cancels it on timeout, so if you place the `withTimeout` on top of `getBluetoothState` and use its scope in it, it should do the proper thing.",
      "parentUuid": "4bdc2f00_26eb2258",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 281,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 281,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "800fca855b5601bbc7ea7df89096a127db720242",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
